# GMEPay+ Test Platform — credential template.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in values for YOUR fleet. This file must only
# ever contain placeholders — never a real secret.
#
# Since the 2026-07-28 security hardening the platform is default-deny, so the tester
# needs three separate credentials. Run `npm run plan` at any time to see which of
# them this environment supplies and exactly which cases each one unblocks. `npm run
# plan` sends no HTTP, so it works with nothing running.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- topology
# Host serving the fleet (ports come from run-fleet.ps1 via src/config.ts).
#GMEPAY_HOST=localhost

# Canonical Keycloak realm. The browser issuer IS the token `iss`, so this same URL
# is used for the token request. Keycloak listens on host port 8097 (8090 is
# scheme-adapter-zeropay — the stale Java default points there and 401s everything).
#GMEPAY_OIDC_ISSUER=http://localhost:8097/realms/gmepay

# ------------------------------------------------- 1. OIDC operator credential
# Opens ops-partner-bff `/v1/admin/**`. Authorization is claim-driven: the token's
# `permissions` claim must carry a platform-operator permission (reads), or one of
# ops:operate / partner.activate / rbac.manage / approval.cfo_override /
# settlement.resolve_exception (writes).
#
# NOTE there is NO client-credentials grant: both seeded SPA clients are public+PKCE
# with serviceAccountsEnabled=false. Use either a token you minted elsewhere...
#GMEPAY_ADMIN_TOKEN=
# ...or the OAuth2 password grant with a realm user.
#GMEPAY_ADMIN_USERNAME=
#GMEPAY_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ------------------------------------------------- 2. OIDC partner credential
# Opens ops-partner-bff `/v1/portal/{partnerCode}/**`. The token's `partner_id` claim
# must MATCH the partner in the path — X-Partner-Id is ignored now, so scope cannot be
# forged. Set GMEPAY_PORTAL_PARTNER_CODE to whatever this user's claim carries.
#GMEPAY_PARTNER_TOKEN=
#GMEPAY_PARTNER_USERNAME=
#GMEPAY_PARTNER_PASSWORD=
#GMEPAY_PORTAL_PARTNER_CODE=GMEREMIT

# ------------------------------------------------- 3. Internal service token
# The `X-Gme-Internal` shared token. Required by every gated /internal/** surface,
# plus prefunding's whole /v1/prefunding/** API, auth-identity's /v1/rbac/** and
# /v1/approvals/**, and kyb-adapter's /v1/kyb/screen.
#
# It must byte-match the value the fleet was booted with. auth-identity, prefunding,
# scheme-adapter-zeropay and rate-fx REFUSE TO START without it — so if those services
# are up, a value exists and you need the same one.
#GMEPAY_INTERNAL_AUTH_SECRET=

# ------------------------------------------------- 4. Partner edge credential
# For the api-gateway HMAC edge. The published stub pair pk_test_abc / sk_test_xyz was
# deleted from src/main and now correctly 401s — it is NOT a usable value.
#
# To provision a real one: POST /internal/auth/keys on auth-identity (needs the
# internal token above), capture the ONE-TIME sk_… plaintext, then have an operator add
# the matching row to the gateway's `gateway.partner-credentials.partners[]` with its
# partner-id and ip-cidr-ranges. A key present in only one of those two halves fails.
#GMEPAY_PARTNER_API_KEY=
#GMEPAY_PARTNER_HMAC_SECRET=
# Must match the partner the key resolves to, or the edge answers 403 PARTNER_ID_MISMATCH.
#GMEPAY_PARTNER_CODE=GMEREMIT
